{:edb/db-before-t 2075 :edb/db-after-t 2076 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535388 50 #inst "2026-10-08T23:15:53.032Z" 13194139535388 true] [17592186087825 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347009 13194139535388 true] [17592186087825 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347023 13194139535388 true] [17592186087826 1020 #edb/ref 17592186346995 13194139535388 true] [17592186087826 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347016 13194139535388 true] [17592186087827 1020 #edb/ref 17592186347002 13194139535388 true] [17592186346995 1017 #edb/ref 17592186346996 13194139535388 true] [17592186346995 1089 "q-14318" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346995 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535388 true] [17592186346995 1100 "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{yx}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\n$$" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346995 1113 #uuid "229ab31e-f5e5-5234-93bf-ecaf044e3397" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346995 1145 "With $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{yx}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)x}{(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{v{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (\\frac{1}{v}+\\frac{1}{{v}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}v & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{2{v}^{2}} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v|-\\frac{1}{{v}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}|+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =C \\\\ 2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}} & =C\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346997 13194139535388 true] [17592186346996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346998 13194139535388 true] [17592186346996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186346999 13194139535388 true] [17592186346996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347000 13194139535388 true] [17592186346996 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347001 13194139535388 true] [17592186346996 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535388 true] [17592186346996 1041 "selection" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346996 1104 #edb/ref 17592186346998 13194139535388 true] [17592186346996 1110 #uuid "b7cccb1f-65f3-5787-9990-3a1c7d1f77e6" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346997 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{y}{{x}^{2}}|+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}=C" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346997 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186346997 1111 #uuid "acd76bfd-2b48-5555-951d-718d17e96d89" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346998 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}=C" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346998 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186346998 1111 #uuid "a43acb57-ccce-5d10-915d-4ab752711bb4" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346999 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}|+2\\frac{y}{x}=C" 13194139535388 true] [17592186346999 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186346999 1111 #uuid "8a6912e4-ff1e-5b9f-b547-4b40e3187c2e" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347000 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{3}}|-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}}=C" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347000 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347000 1111 #uuid "a8d3d60c-6b7c-536d-8232-0c3fa067f472" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347001 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡|y|-\\frac{y}{x}=C" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347001 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347001 1111 #uuid "d704103b-8247-507d-a7b9-61e183bffa8e" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347002 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347003 13194139535388 true] [17592186347002 1089 "q-14322" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347002 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535388 true] [17592186347002 1100 "Which of the following is NOT a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347002 1113 #uuid "07cbf2f2-d5ef-5e3f-8e63-cd4b2886b3f6" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347002 1145 "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is NOT the case is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}.$\n\nWe see that the numerator is NOT a homogeneous polynomial. Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is NOT a homogeneous function.\n\nHence, the original differential equation is  NOT homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}\\,\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is not homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)\\ne f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\nFor $x=1$, $y=2$ and $t=3$, for instance, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =f(2\\cdot 1,2\\cdot 3) \\\\  & =f(2,6) \\\\  & =\\frac{{2}^{2}+1}{{6}^{2}+2(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{48}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y) & =f(1,2) \\\\  & =\\frac{{1}^{2}+1}{{2}^{2}+1(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn other words, there exists at least one combination of values of $x$, $y$ and $t$ for which the identity $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y)$ is not observed.\n\nHence, the original differential equation is  NOT homogeneous." 13194139535388 true] [17592186347003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347004 13194139535388 true] [17592186347003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347005 13194139535388 true] [17592186347003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347006 13194139535388 true] [17592186347003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347007 13194139535388 true] [17592186347003 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347008 13194139535388 true] [17592186347003 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535388 true] [17592186347003 1041 "selection" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347003 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347005 13194139535388 true] [17592186347003 1110 #uuid "7ff28647-7053-5c93-a365-e7beed2ca160" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347004 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x}{y})}" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347004 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347004 1111 #uuid "6865b4dc-bb1b-58ce-a871-56fabaa9d0b8" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347005 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}+1}{{y}^{2}+xy}" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347005 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347005 1111 #uuid "5c94aa24-b4aa-5294-8d6b-45a136c59aa5" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347006 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{xy}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347006 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347006 1111 #uuid "9be4c937-7a50-5044-be2d-dc56e02f18b9" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347007 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{4{x}^{2}y}{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}}" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347007 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347007 1111 #uuid "886d1cb9-651e-55c3-8dd7-f0cd516ec217" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347008 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{x+y}{y})" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347008 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347008 1111 #uuid "44afc39f-e195-5a49-b77f-1a6b7858a92e" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347009 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347010 13194139535388 true] [17592186347009 1089 "q-14323" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347009 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535388 true] [17592186347009 1100 "Consider the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+2y{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nIf the transformation $y=v(x)x$ is applied to the differential equation, what is the resulting equation?" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347009 1113 #uuid "ac3cbdaf-bfc0-50ab-89f3-54af7a9e11ba" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347009 1145 "Using the transformation $y=vx$ (where $v=v(x)$), we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given differential equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+x{y}^{2}-{y}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+2y{x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}+x(vx)^{2}-(vx)^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+2(vx){x}^{2}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}(1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3})}{{x}^{3}({v}^{2}+2v)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}-{v}^{3}-2{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+2v} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+2v}{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347011 13194139535388 true] [17592186347010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347012 13194139535388 true] [17592186347010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347013 13194139535388 true] [17592186347010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347014 13194139535388 true] [17592186347010 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347015 13194139535388 true] [17592186347010 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535388 true] [17592186347010 1041 "selection" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347010 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347013 13194139535388 true] [17592186347010 1110 #uuid "2a51ca83-20ab-506e-8203-e11a1404252a" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347011 1034 "\\frac{{v}^{3}+2{v}^{2}}{1-{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347011 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347011 1111 #uuid "49a1ff16-6933-5a69-a8ae-d7cff266954f" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347012 1034 "\\frac{v+2}{1-3v-2{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347012 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347012 1111 #uuid "877429e0-f6c3-5e38-ac9e-9a63efc0ed8b" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347013 1034 "\\frac{{v}^{2}+2v}{1-{v}^{2}-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347013 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347013 1111 #uuid "8c75faa8-297d-53b1-a93d-56bbf35438ee" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347014 1034 "\\frac{1-2v-3{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+2v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347014 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347014 1111 #uuid "19c39017-c049-534c-be7c-e97383d4c2dd" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347015 1034 "\\frac{{v}^{2}-1}{1-2{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347015 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347015 1111 #uuid "cfb88851-5f78-508f-b23e-65272f51e213" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347016 1017 #edb/ref 17592186347017 13194139535388 true] [17592186347016 1089 "q-8845" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347016 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535388 true] [17592186347016 1100 "Use the transformation $y=v(x)x$ to find the general solution of the following homogeneous differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})+1)\n$$" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347016 1113 #uuid "1a788c8d-223d-5e9b-9a2b-46f1e25dd2ff" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347016 1145 "With $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{y}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})+1) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{vx}{x}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{vx}{x})+1) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =v(\\operatorname{ln}⁡v+1) \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v+v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v \\\\ \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTo evaluate the integral on the left-hand side, we use integration by substitution with\n\n$$\nu=\\operatorname{ln}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=\\frac{1}{v}.\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to solve the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{v\\operatorname{ln}⁡v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{u}\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡v| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into our solution, we finally obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡v| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{e}^{C} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{C}|x|) \\\\ |\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x}| & =|x|{e}^{C} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x} & =\\pm {e}^{C}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{y}{x} & =Kx \\\\ \\frac{y}{x} & ={e}^{Kx} \\\\ y & =x{e}^{Kx}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced the new constant of integration:\n\n$$\nK=\\pm {e}^{C}\n$$" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347018 13194139535388 true] [17592186347017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347019 13194139535388 true] [17592186347017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347020 13194139535388 true] [17592186347017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347021 13194139535388 true] [17592186347017 1000 #edb/ref 17592186347022 13194139535388 true] [17592186347017 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535388 true] [17592186347017 1041 "selection" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347017 1104 #edb/ref 17592186347018 13194139535388 true] [17592186347017 1110 #uuid "f578f94a-1131-5692-995d-02a333ecc2f1" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347018 1034 "y=x{e}^{Kx}" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347018 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535388 true] [17592186347018 1111 #uuid "72bfbf59-db54-5c23-9b71-10aa88eece49" 13194139535388 true] [17592186347019 1034 "y=K{x}^{2}